  "text_input": "The patient was apparently normal 2 days back. Then she developed easy fatigability × 2 days. Patient felt tired on performing routine daily activities, which were previously well tolerated.\nHistory of unresponsiveness: it was sudden in onset . It was noticed by her daughter at home. The patient was not responding to verbal/painful stimuli. The episode lasted for around 15 minutes and was associated with loss of consciousness but aware of surroundings. There was involuntary movement of upper limbs.\nNo similar history.\nNo history of head injury\nNo history of involuntary seizures (tongue bite, bowel/bladder incontinence, frothing from mouth)\nNo post-ictal confusion\nNo up-rolling of eyes\nNo history of chest pain, palpitations, breathlessness.\nNo history of blurring of vision, headache, head trauma.\nNo history of fever, altered sensorium, or burning micturition.\nNo history of abdominal pain.",
